title The deepest body, and the first family the queue found rather than a hand
prompt Autonomous loop -- read the voice and style canon, then REMEMBER and the itineraries, close open reds first, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, read one council-rota row, send each finished increment as its own signed round
think Standfast first. crux/REDS.md reads %144 and %145 both booked and CLOSED, with no living row open, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread came off the newest log's recommend line: mind_the_impasse leads the ranked queue at 350 over eight rungs of a fifty-three-line body, the first row the queue found rather than a hand kept.
think Measured before cutting. tools/fixtures/ladder_reach_visibility_scan.sh mind_the_impasse read declared=9 identical=8 lines=53 stub=3 fall=350 widens=0, matching the pinned row exactly.
think Read the ninth declaration before assuming drift. caravan/mind.rye writes the same fifty-three lines reaching report_out.minded, report_out.unminded, and report_out.begun directly, where the other eight reach them through mind_of(report_out). That is a different report shape rather than a stale copy, so mind.rye keeps its own body -- the visibility-split lesson of REDS %144 read one level over, on record structure rather than on a keyword.
think Lifted the body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye as pub fn mind_the_impasse(comptime rung: type, io: std.Io, mind: rung.Mind, report_out: *rung.Report) (rung.RunError || rung.NoteError)!void, seated directly after redress_the_meeting among the movement rungs it runs beside. Every free symbol became rung-qualified: hold_standing, holds_rest, mind_of, unminded_impasses, minded_in, begun_in, max_address_len, address_published, addressable, rest_written, holds_carries, mind_refusal, mind_note, mind_holds, mind_published, minds_bytes, clear_forbear. Both // invariant: asserts travelled with the body, all six of them.
think Each of the eight rungs now calls it through a three-line stub keeping its own doc comment, the same shape the arc has used for every lift.
think Carry 60,510 -> 60,160, a fall of 350 -- the number the scan's formula returned before the lap began, eight laps running. Lowered the ceiling in both tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish and the scan default.
think Rotated the pins. The folded row moved from appraisal_note to mind_the_impasse; the queue head fell to suits_path at 350 with examined=47; the sink window fell 65,820 -> 65,420 total and 64,680 -> 64,280 above the line, since a lifted body leaves the rungs rather than the harness. farewell.rye's holding fell 3,876 -> 3,826.
think tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish refused the first narrative rewrite: it spelled fifty-three and four in prose with no assert holding either number. The guard is right -- a recited number drifts the moment the tree moves under it -- so both narratives now say the shape in words and leave every number to the asserts.
obs The finding worth carrying is that the ordering correction paid off one lap after it landed. REDS %145 replaced a hand-kept shortlist with an exact ranking, and the very next lap lifted a family that shortlist could never have reached: eight rungs is narrow, and carry multiplies rungs by whole lines. A correction to a meter returns nothing on the lap it lands and everything on the lap after.
obs The second finding is that a ninth declaration standing outside an identical family is worth reading before it is called drift. mind.rye differs in exactly one thing -- whether the report holds the minding counts directly or behind mind_of -- and that is meaning. A lift that had forced it into the family would have published a sub-record one rung deliberately does without.
obs The council rota row read this lap was Air and Saturn -- law and boundary. Single-strandedness landed directly: a body written in eight places is eight threads a reader must hold, and one published function with eight three-line stubs is one. Conway's Law read harder still -- the whole arc exists because sessions share no memory, so a rule written once in a file is a rule the next session cannot come to disagree with, where a rule written eight times is eight chances for the channel to fray.
